The fermionic operator $a_{i}^{\dagger }a_{j}^{\dagger }a_{k}a_{l}$ expands
in terms of Majorana operators as

\begin{align*}
a_{i}^{\dagger }a_{j}^{\dagger }a_{k}a_{l}& =\frac{1}{16}\left\{ \left( 
\overset{}{%
x_{j}x_{k}x_{l}x_{m}+x_{j}x_{k}x_{l+r}x_{m+r}-x_{j}x_{k+r}x_{l}x_{m+r}+x_{j}x_{k+r}x_{l+r}x_{m}%
}\right. \right.  \\
& \left. \overset{}{%
-x_{j+r}x_{k}x_{l+r}x_{m}+x_{j+r}x_{k}x_{l}x_{m+r}+x_{j+r}x_{k+r}x_{l}x_{m}+x_{j+r}x_{k+r}x_{l+r}x_{m+r}%
}\right)  \\
& i\left( \overset{}{%
+x_{j}x_{k}x_{l}x_{m+r}-x_{j}x_{k}x_{l+r}x_{m}+x_{j}x_{k+r}x_{l}x_{m}+x_{j}x_{k+r}x_{l+r}x_{m+r}%
}\right.  \\
& \left. \left. \overset{}{%
-x_{j+r}x_{k}x_{l}x_{m}-x_{j+r}x_{k}x_{l+r}x_{m+r}+x_{j+r}x_{k+r}x_{l}x_{m+r}-x_{j+r}x_{k+r}x_{l+r}x_{m}%
}\right) \right\} 
\end{align*}

where $x _{j}$ are Majorana operators satisfying $\{x _{j},x _{k}\}=2\delta
_{jk}$, with the fermionic mapping 
\begin{align*}
a_{j}& =\tfrac{1}{2}(x _{j}+ix _{j+r}) \\
a_{j}^{\dagger }& =\tfrac{1}{2}(x _{j}-ix _{j+r})
\end{align*}

